[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Metric and Bucket Aggregations in Elasticsearch"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Elasticsearch aggregations bring immense power to data analysis, allowing you to build complex summaries and statistical reports out of your indexed documents. Aggregations fall primarily into two main categories: Bucket Aggregations and Metric Aggregations."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Bucket Aggregations"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Bucket aggregations do not calculate statistics directly. Instead, they create buckets, or partitions, of documents based on specific criteria. As documents pass through the aggregation, Elasticsearch evaluates the field values and sorts them into corresponding buckets."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Terms Aggregation: Dynamically builds a bucket for each unique value found in a field."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Date Histogram Aggregation: Groups documents into chronological intervals like days, months, or years."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Range Aggregation: Groups documents into custom ranges defined by the user."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Metric Aggregations"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Metric aggregations, unlike buckets, mathematically calculate values—such as sums, averages, minimums, and maximums—from the fields of the documents. They act on the documents contained within a specific bucket."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Avg, Min, Max, and Sum: Basic arithmetic metrics."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Stats: Returns count, min, max, average, and sum all in a single response."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Cardinality: Calculates an approximate count of distinct values."},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Combining Buckets and Metrics"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"The true strength of Elasticsearch aggregations is nesting. You can place metric aggregations inside bucket aggregations to compute statistics for each individual bucket. For example, you can group sales records by region (bucket) and calculate the total revenue for each region (metric)."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"GET /sales/_search
{
  "size": 0,
  "aggs": {
    "genres_bucket": {
      "terms": {
        "field": "genre"
      },
      "aggs": {
        "avg_price": {
          "avg": {
            "field": "price"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"In the query above, the "genres_bucket" creates buckets for every distinct movie genre, and the nested "avg_price" metric calculates the average price of items within each specific genre bucket."}]
